{"success": true, "name": "arc-stream-review", "file": "references/periodic-row-sequence.md", "content": "# Periodic row-sequence demonstrations

When a demo contains a compact non-background motif and the test contains full-width rows of single colors, consider whether the task is sequence extrapolation across rows rather than a cell-local transformation. Read the input/output row-by-row, identify unchanged rows and inserted/recolored rows, and infer any cycle only after checking the complete output. Apply the resulting sequence to the test's row structure and verify every row, including the cycle boundary; do not assume original test rows are all preserved as markers.

For the reviewed example, the 5x5 input rows were `1,9,7,0,0`; `9,1,9,7,0`; `0,9,1,9,7`; `0,0,9,1,9`; `0,0,0,9,1`. The output continued/filled the row-wise periodic pattern so each row became a repeated sequence of colors, with row starts cycling `1,9,7,9,1`. This is a clue to test row-cycle extrapolation, not sufficient alone to assert a unique rule for a different test.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1790545217/attempts/771c27e3136742b79bef1ff131c04e1e/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/arc-stream-review/references/periodic-row-sequence.md"}
